# Core layout for a Docker VM with 20 vCPUs (a 14-core / 20-thread laptop).
# vCPUs 0-1 stay free for the VM itself (dockerd, the kernel, the network).
# Sluice gets two vCPUs and a quota of SLUICE_CPUS: with cpus=1 Go runs
# GOMAXPROCS=2 under a 1-CPU quota, as in a 1-CPU container on a larger VPS.
# For SLUICE_CPUS=2 use SLUICE_CPUSET=2-5.
SLUICE_CPUSET=2,3
DB_CPUSET=6-9
ISSUER_CPUSET=10,11
PROXY_CPUSET=12,13
RUNNER_CPUSET=14-19
